      <div type="clause" n="70">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 70</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa cwydeleas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.13-2"/> of þysu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life gewíte, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.14-2"/> hit þurh his gymeleaste, si hit þurh færlicne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.15"/> deað, þonne ne teo se hlaford<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.16"/> na mare on his æhta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.17"/> butan his rihtan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.18"/> heregeata.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hergeate. Gyf of ðysum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.3"/> life man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.4"/> gewíte cwydeleas, sy hit ðurh his gymelyste, sy hyt ðurh færlicne deaþ, ðonne ne teo se laford nan mare on his æhte butan his rihtan heregeate.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa cwydeleas of þissu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life gewite, sy hyt þurh his gymeleaste, sy hit þurh fearlicne deað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, þonne ne teo se hlaford na mare on his æhte butan his rihte heregeate.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis quideles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.9"/> ex hac uita discesserit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.10"/> (decedat sine distributione rerum suarum), uel per incustodiam uel per mortem inprouisam, non usurpet sibi dominus eius de pecunia sua nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.11"/> quantum ad iustam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.12"/> releuationem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.13"/> pertinet (quę Anglice uocatur héregeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.14"/>).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis obmutescit, antequam ex hac uita exeat, seu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.8"/> per neglegentiam seu per subitam mortem, dominus eius nichil se intromittat de omnibus bonis illius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.9-2"/>, nisi quantum ad eum iuste pertinet, hoc est tantum quod Angli uocant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.10-2"/> heregeate.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_70.lnote.oe.11-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="70" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis forte sine detestacione ex hac uita migrauerit, siue propter in[c]uriam siue propter mortem subitaneam, dominus illius non uendicet sibi quicquam amplius de ipsius possessione nisi sua iusta excercitualia.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="70" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>Be hergeate. Gyf of ðysum life man<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_70.robnote.fn.10"/> gewíte cwydeleas, sy hit ðurh his gymelyste, sy hyt ðurh færlicne deaþ, ðonne ne teo se laford nan mare on his æhte butan his rihtan heregeate.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="288" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hwa cwydeleas of þysum life gewite, si hit þurh his gymeleaste, si hit þurh færlicne deað, þonne ne teo se hlaford na mare on his æhta butan his rihtan heregeata.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>(Über ‘Hergewæte’.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.1"/> <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und wenn einer (jemand <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) ohne letztwillige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.2"/> Verfügung [für Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.3"/> und Herrn] aus diesem Leben scheidet, sei es [sie unterblieb] durch seine Nachlässigkeit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.4"/>, sei es durch plötzlichen Tod, dann nehme aus dessen Fahrhabe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.5"/> der Herr nicht(s <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) mehr als sein richtiges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_70.lnote.de.6"/> ‘Hergewæte’ [Kriegsrüstung].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Concerning heriot. B) And if anyone (someone, B) departs this life without a last disposition [for church and lord], whether [it was left undone] through his negligence or through sudden death, then let the lord take from his movable goods no(thing, B) more than his proper heriot [war-gear].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning heriots<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_70.robnote.n.1"/>. If a man departs from this life intestate, whether through negligence or through sudden death, his lord shall take no more from his property than his legal heriot.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone departs from this life intestate, be it through his heedlessness, or through sudden death, the lord is then not to take more from his possessions than his legal heriot.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="289" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone passes away without having made a will, either because of negligence or sudden death, the lord shall take no more from his estate than his legal tribute.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_20">Leis Wl 20–20.3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 357, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
