        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dicunt <hi rend="italic">Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dicunt Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">herg. <hi rend="italic">HDi;</hi> heregeat <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> heregete <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">herg. HDi; heregeat Cb; heregete Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ein Abschnitt umfasst 70—71, 5. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Heergewäte; Testament 2; Erbgang 9c. d. 15aff. Die Sätze 70. 70, 1 benutzt aus Inst Bracton II 26, f. 60b = Fleta II 57, 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">One section comprises 70—71, 5. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Heergewäte; Testament 2; Erbgang 9c. d. 15aff. Sentences 70. 70, 1 are used, from Inst, by Bracton II 26, f. 60b = Fleta II 57, 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">detestare</hi> statt <hi rend="italic">testari</hi> Ducange; daher C <hi rend="italic">detestatio</hi> statt <hi rend="italic">testamentum</hi>. Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> liess das Wort als unverstanden unübersetzt; Inst missverstand ‘sprachlos’, vielleicht verführt durch <hi rend="italic">obmutesco</hi> des Juristen-Lateins</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">detestare</hi> for <hi rend="italic">testari</hi> Ducange; hence C <hi rend="italic">detestatio</hi> for <hi rend="italic">testamentum</hi>. Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> left the word untranslated as not understood; Inst misunderstood it as ‘speechless’, perhaps misled by the <hi rend="italic">obmutesco</hi> of lawyers’ Latin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zahlreiche Testamente, die beide bedenken, sind erhalten. Direkten Einfluss Röm. Rechts auf Cnut, den Savigny behauptete, leugnet Conrat (Cohn) <hi rend="italic">Gesch. Röm. Rechts</hi> I 60</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Numerous wills providing for both have survived. A direct influence of Roman law on Cnut, which Savigny asserted, is denied by Conrat (Cohn) <hi rend="italic">Gesch. Röm. Rechts</hi> I 60</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht für die Seele zu sorgen gilt schon damals als nachlässig; <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Pol Mai I 108</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Failure to provide for one’s soul was already then regarded as negligent; <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. Pol Mai I 108</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 78 steht <hi rend="italic">land</hi> geschieden von <hi rend="italic">æhtan</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Below</hi> 78 <hi rend="italic">land</hi> is distinguished from <hi rend="italic">æhtan</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_70.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. setzt Cnut eine Ausnahme von Heergewätepflicht fest</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Cnut lays down an exception to the obligation of heriot</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_70.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See P. and M. <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. p. 312 ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_70.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>man</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">And gif hwa cw.</hi> &amp;c. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
